From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:28:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Android: rfd and arboard shims, no ArtCraft marks
 (DexPdfCraft fork)

PdfCraft's egui interface builds for Android (aarch64-linux-android):

- android/rfd-shim and android/arboard-shim take the names rfd and arboard
  for pdfcraft-ui-egui. On every other target they re-export the real crates,
  so nothing changes there; on Android they implement the subset of the API
  the interface uses and are answered by backends the app installs (the
  Storage Access Framework and ClipboardManager). Without a backend, pickers
  are cancelled and the clipboard stays inside the process.
- The ArtCraft wordmark and mark are trademarks that forks must remove
  (docs/brand/LICENSE-brand.txt): artcraft_logo shows the program's name in
  plain text and artcraft_mark leaves empty space; no brand file is embedded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
